# Reference Point — Gap Card Label (`.g-label`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a gap/problem card label (e.g. "Certifications buyers can't read"), match `.g-label` in `.gap-card` inside `#problem`.

## Structure

```html
<article class="gap-card">
  <p class="g-label">Short gap name</p>
  <h3>Italic serif headline.</h3>
  <hr /><p class="lead">Supporting detail sentence.</p>
</article>
```

Place inside `.gap-grid` under `.gaps-block` / `#problem`.

## Visual spec

| Layer | Class | Treatment |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| Card | `.gap-card` | white bg, `var(--border)`, 16px radius, column flex, `gap: 0.75rem` |
| Label | `.g-label` | `0.8125rem`, weight 500, `0.05em` tracking, uppercase, `#8c6b66` |
| Headline | `h3` | `var(--serif)`, italic, weight 400, `var(--ink)` |
| Divider | `hr` | 1px `var(--border)` |
| Body | `.lead` | `var(--muted)`, `var(--body)` in overview, line-height 1.6 |

## vs other labels

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `.g-label` | Gap card top label — muted brown `#8c6b66` |
| `.eyebrow.soft` | Section subsection label — grey |
| `.col-label` | About column label — `var(--label)` brown |
| `.eyebrow` | Main section label — brown, wider tracking |

## Do not

- Use inline styles on `.g-label` — remove overrides; use base class only.
- Swap `.g-label` for `.eyebrow.soft` on gap cards — different color and size.
- Use `.display` or `h3.title` for the card headline — keep plain `h3` italic inside cards.
